  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AR Engendering African Social Movements</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding the En(gender)ing African Social Movements Project to build the capacity of member movements of
Africans Rising to mainstream gender equality and its intersection with climate justice into their operations at all
levels. The project will alsoincorporatecampaigns at grassroots level, connecting movement members and building
solidarity among movements across borders to advocate for women&apos;s reproductive rights, economic rights and
climate justice. All advocacy and capacity building under thisproject will take intersectional approach especially as
climate change currently affects a greater proportion of women in Africa. This project contributesto the pathway on
building Strong, inclusive climate movements in Africa.

En(gender)ing AfricanSocial Movements has achieved greatsuccess since its inception. Through the project, we have
developed a Feminist Curriculum that outlines the feminist principles andtheir application to build an inclusive
society. It has enabled us to convene, connect, empower and support movements to build capacity as they work to
dismantle oppressive systems interlinking gender inequality, climate crisis, poverty, political and social exclusion. We
have also started training and capacity building of Africans Rising Core Team and Coordinating Collective and will
reach more movements this year through campaigns during International Women&apos;s Day, 16 days of activism, Invisible
giants recognition, movement exchange, 25th May mobilisation. The expansion of the project is a sudden
opportunity given the need to accelerate campaigns andactions against climate polluters and especially to push for
loss and damage. In communities where climate change has led to devastation of the environment or led to extreme
weatherevents, women have been the most affected. It is necessary to ensure that in tackling this catastrophe,
women&apos;s rights and inclusion are at integrated in movement work and actions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="23">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Africans Rising is a Pan-African movement of people and organisations, working for peace, justice, and dignity.
Africans Rising looks to play a critical role on the continent pushing governments, business, and even established global and national NGOs to focus onchallenges African&#x2019;s deem critical, including demands for a fair global trading system, concrete action to address the effects of climate change and the creation and strengthening of a representative coalition to protect our natural resources and the environment.
Africans Rising has a specific focus on issues including:
&#x2022; Expanding space for civic and political action
&#x2022; Fighting for women&#x2019;s rights and freedoms across society
&#x2022; Focusing on the right to equity and dignity
&#x2022; Ensuring good democratic and corruption-free governance
&#x2022; Promoting climate and environmental justice</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AfricansRising forJustice,Peace &amp;Di</narrative>
  </participating-org>
